https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/60bed5fc-0712-415d-acf8-a1cc4360aeec

Clicking `b` will `Hide/Show` the last button that has 2 tooltips, everything works as expected no?

I was just checking around and the https://github.com/ebitenui/ebitenui/blob/master/_examples/widget_demos/imagebutton/main.go is not working as expected, and if I comment the code I added on this PR it works :shrug: 

At the end the issue is the `fireEvents()` that it should not be done (as it fires the Click)

Doing something like:

```diff
diff --git a/widget/widget.go b/widget/widget.go
index ac87fe2..a7447f9 100644
--- a/widget/widget.go
+++ b/widget/widget.go
@@ -646,10 +646,9 @@ func (w *Widget) Render(screen *ebiten.Image) {
 }
 
 func (w *Widget) Update(updObj *UpdateObject) {
-       if !w.IsVisible() {
-               return
+       if w.IsVisible() {
+               w.fireEvents()
        }
-       w.fireEvents()
        if w.DragAndDrop != nil {
                w.DragAndDrop.Update(w.self)
        }
```

Makes it work, basically only firing events if it's visible, the res of the `Update` is still run.
